From: christopherrobertbrooks-tech
 <289533927+christopherrobertbrooks-tech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:27:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cuda): compute the lyric encoder's last projection in
 float32 on float16 GPUs

On GPUs without bfloat16 (Volta, Turing, Pascal) the model runs in float16, and the lyric
encoder's last MLP projection reaches ~505,000 on ordinary lyrics -- past float16's 65,504 --
so every latent turns NaN for songs with lyrics while instrumentals work (#1055, #1243; see also
the closed PR #1274).

Only that projection is computed in float32, from its own float16 weights upcast on the fly
(autocast disabled); the final norm's output is cast back to the model dtype. No weights are
changed or copied. The fix lives in a new module (fp16_lyric_encoder.py); the loader calls it
only when the model dtype is float16, and it logs a warning if the encoder is not recognised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
